---@field reportArn? aws.codebuild.NonEmptyString The ARN of the report to which the test case belongs.
---@field testRawDataPath? aws.codebuild.String The path to the raw data file that contains the test result.
---@field prefix? aws.codebuild.String A string that is applied to a series of related test cases. CodeBuild generates the prefix. The prefix depends on the framework used to generate the tests.
---@field name? aws.codebuild.String The name of the test case.
---@field status? aws.codebuild.String The status returned by the test case after it was run. Valid statuses are SUCCEEDED, FAILED, ERROR, SKIPPED, and UNKNOWN.
---@field durationInNanoSeconds? aws.codebuild.WrapperLong The number of nanoseconds it took to run this test case.
---@field message? aws.codebuild.String A message associated with a test case. For example, an error message or stack trace.
---@field expired? aws.codebuild.Timestamp The date and time a test case expires. A test case expires 30 days after it is created. An expired test case is not available to view in CodeBuild.
---@field testSuiteName? aws.codebuild.String The name of the test suite that the test case is a part of.

---A filter used to return specific types of test cases. In order to pass the filter, the report must meet all of the filter properties.
