---@class aws.codebuild.UpdateProjectInput
---@field name aws.codebuild.NonEmptyString The name of the build project.
---@field description? aws.codebuild.ProjectDescription A new or replacement description of the build project.
---@field source? aws.codebuild.ProjectSource Information to be changed about the build input source code for the build project.
---@field secondarySources? aws.codebuild.ProjectSources An array of ProjectSource objects.
---@field sourceVersion? aws.codebuild.String A version of the build input to be built for this project. If not specified, the latest version is used. If specified, it must be one of:
---@field secondarySourceVersions? aws.codebuild.ProjectSecondarySourceVersions An array of ProjectSourceVersion objects. If secondarySourceVersions is specified at the build level, then they take over these secondarySourceVersions (at the project level).
---@field artifacts? aws.codebuild.ProjectArtifacts Information to be changed about the build output artifacts for the build project.
---@field secondaryArtifacts? aws.codebuild.ProjectArtifactsList An array of ProjectArtifact objects.
---@field cache? aws.codebuild.ProjectCache Stores recently used information so that it can be quickly accessed at a later time.
---@field environment? aws.codebuild.ProjectEnvironment Information to be changed about the build environment for the build project.
---@field serviceRole? aws.codebuild.NonEmptyString The replacement ARN of the IAM role that enables CodeBuild to interact with dependent Amazon Web Services services on behalf of the Amazon Web Services account.
---@field timeoutInMinutes? aws.codebuild.BuildTimeOut The replacement value in minutes, from 5 to 2160 (36 hours), for CodeBuild to wait before timing out any related build that did not get marked as completed.
---@field queuedTimeoutInMinutes? aws.codebuild.TimeOut The number of minutes a build is allowed to be queued before it times out.
---@field encryptionKey? aws.codebuild.NonEmptyString The Key Management Service customer master key (CMK) to be used for encrypting the build output artifacts.
---@field tags? aws.codebuild.TagList An updated list of tag key and value pairs associated with this build project.
---@field vpcConfig? aws.codebuild.VpcConfig VpcConfig enables CodeBuild to access resources in an Amazon VPC.
---@field badgeEnabled? aws.codebuild.WrapperBoolean Set this to true to generate a publicly accessible URL for your project's build badge.
---@field logsConfig? aws.codebuild.LogsConfig Information about logs for the build project. A project can create logs in CloudWatch Logs, logs in an S3 bucket, or both.
---@field fileSystemLocations? aws.codebuild.ProjectFileSystemLocations An array of ProjectFileSystemLocation objects for a CodeBuild build project. A ProjectFileSystemLocation object specifies the identifier, location, mountOptions, mountPoint, and type of a file system created using Amazon Elastic File System.
---@field buildBatchConfig? aws.codebuild.ProjectBuildBatchConfig
---@field concurrentBuildLimit? aws.codebuild.WrapperInt The maximum number of concurrent builds that are allowed for this project.
---@field autoRetryLimit? aws.codebuild.WrapperInt The maximum number of additional automatic retries after a failed build. For example, if the auto-retry limit is set to 2, CodeBuild will call the RetryBuild API to automatically retry your build for up to 2 additional times.

