---@class aws.codebuild.UpdateWebhookInput
---@field projectName aws.codebuild.ProjectName The name of the CodeBuild project.
---@field branchFilter? aws.codebuild.String A regular expression used to determine which repository branches are built when a webhook is triggered. If the name of a branch matches the regular expression, then it is built. If branchFilter is empty, then all branches are built.
---@field rotateSecret? aws.codebuild.Boolean A boolean value that specifies whether the associated GitHub repository's secret token should be updated. If you use Bitbucket for your repository, rotateSecret is ignored.
---@field filterGroups? aws.codebuild.FilterGroups An array of arrays of WebhookFilter objects used to determine if a webhook event can trigger a build. A filter group must contain at least one EVENT WebhookFilter.
---@field buildType? aws.codebuild.WebhookBuildType|string Specifies the type of build this webhook will trigger.
---@field pullRequestBuildPolicy? aws.codebuild.PullRequestBuildPolicy A PullRequestBuildPolicy object that defines comment-based approval requirements for triggering builds on pull requests. This policy helps control when automated builds are executed based on contributor permissions and approval workflows.

---@class aws.codebuild.UpdateWebhookOutput
---@field webhook? aws.codebuild.Webhook Information about a repository's webhook that is associated with a project in CodeBuild.

---@alias aws.codebuild.ValueInput string

---Information about the VPC configuration that CodeBuild accesses.
---@class aws.codebuild.VpcConfig
---@field vpcId? aws.codebuild.NonEmptyString The ID of the Amazon VPC.
---@field subnets? aws.codebuild.Subnets A list of one or more subnet IDs in your Amazon VPC.
---@field securityGroupIds? aws.codebuild.SecurityGroupIds A list of one or more security groups IDs in your Amazon VPC.

---Information about a webhook that connects repository events to a build project in CodeBuild.
---@class aws.codebuild.Webhook
---@field url? aws.codebuild.NonEmptyString The URL to the webhook.
---@field payloadUrl? aws.codebuild.NonEmptyString The CodeBuild endpoint where webhook events are sent.
---@field secret? aws.codebuild.NonEmptyString The secret token of the associated repository.
---@field branchFilter? aws.codebuild.String A regular expression used to determine which repository branches are built when a webhook is triggered. If the name of a branch matches the regular expression, then it is built. If branchFilter is empty, then all branches are built.
---@field filterGroups? aws.codebuild.FilterGroups An array of arrays of WebhookFilter objects used to determine which webhooks are triggered. At least one WebhookFilter in the array must specify EVENT as its type.
---@field buildType? aws.codebuild.WebhookBuildType Specifies the type of build this webhook will trigger.
---@field manualCreation? aws.codebuild.WrapperBoolean If manualCreation is true, CodeBuild doesn't create a webhook in GitHub and instead returns payloadUrl and secret values for the webhook. The payloadUrl and secret values in the output can be used to manually create a webhook within GitHub.
---@field lastModifiedSecret? aws.codebuild.Timestamp A timestamp that indicates the last time a repository's secret token was modified.
---@field scopeConfiguration? aws.codebuild.ScopeConfiguration The scope configuration for global or organization webhooks.
---@field status? aws.codebuild.WebhookStatus The status of the webhook. Valid values include:
---@field statusMessage? aws.codebuild.String A message associated with the status of a webhook.
---@field pullRequestBuildPolicy? aws.codebuild.PullRequestBuildPolicy

---@alias aws.codebuild.WebhookBuildType "BUILD"|"BUILD_BATCH"|"RUNNER_BUILDKITE_BUILD"

---A filter used to determine which webhooks trigger a build.
---@class aws.codebuild.WebhookFilter
---@field type aws.codebuild.WebhookFilterType|string The type of webhook filter. There are 11 webhook filter types: EVENT, ACTOR_ACCOUNT_ID, HEAD_REF, BASE_REF, FILE_PATH, COMMIT_MESSAGE, TAG_NAME, RELEASE_NAME, REPOSITORY_NAME, ORGANIZATION_NAME, and WORKFLOW_NAME.
---@field pattern aws.codebuild.String For a WebHookFilter that uses EVENT type, a comma-separated string that specifies one or more events. For example, the webhook filter PUSH, PULL_REQUEST_CREATED, PULL_REQUEST_UPDATED allows all push, pull request created, and pull request updated events to trigger a build.
---@field excludeMatchedPattern? aws.codebuild.WrapperBoolean Used to indicate that the pattern determines which webhook events do not trigger a build. If true, then a webhook event that does not match the pattern triggers a build. If false, then a webhook event that matches the pattern triggers a build.

---@alias aws.codebuild.WebhookFilterType "EVENT"|"BASE_REF"|"HEAD_REF"|"ACTOR_ACCOUNT_ID"|"FILE_PATH"|"COMMIT_MESSAGE"|"WORKFLOW_NAME"|"TAG_NAME"|"RELEASE_NAME"|"REPOSITORY_NAME"|"ORGANIZATION_NAME"

---@alias aws.codebuild.WebhookScopeType "GITHUB_ORGANIZATION"|"GITHUB_GLOBAL"|"GITLAB_GROUP"

---@alias aws.codebuild.WebhookStatus "CREATING"|"CREATE_FAILED"|"ACTIVE"|"DELETING"

---@alias aws.codebuild.WrapperBoolean boolean

